Spatchcocked Roast Chicken with Quick Jus
Serves: 6
Prep: 15 min
Cook: 50 min
Total: 1 hr 5 min, plus optional 3–24 hr dry brine
Equipment: Kitchen shears, Wire rack, Rimmed baking sheet, Foil, Small saucepan, Fine-mesh strainer, Instant-read thermometer

Carve: Rest the chicken **5 min** under loose foil. Carve and serve with the hot jus.
  Roast (heat, ~45 min): Rub oil over the skin. Roast to **66 °C** in the breast near the bone and **80 °C** at the thigh joint.
    Season: Mix and sprinkle over skin and cavity. Skin up on a rack over a foil-lined sheet, breasts centred. Optional: fridge **uncovered 3–24 hr**.
      Stuff: Gently loosen the skin over breast and thighs without tearing. Push herbs underneath evenly.
        Flatten: Oven to **230 °C / 450 °F**, rack upper-middle. Cut out the backbone with shears, chop it into **2.5 cm** pieces and keep it. Press the breastbone flat.
          - 1 | Large chicken | 1.8–2.3 kg · 4–5 lb
        Chop: Pick the leaves and chop to about **2 tsp**.
          - small handful | Fresh herbs | any mix · optional
      - 15 g = 1 Tbsp | Kosher salt | weigh other salts
      - ½ tsp | Black pepper
      - 1 tsp | Baking powder | optional, for crisper skin
    - 1 Tbsp | Neutral oil
  Whisk (combine): **Off the heat**, whisk in soy and butter. Squeeze in the lemon. Season.
    Simmer (heat, ~27 min): Add bay, vermouth and water; scrape the pan. Simmer **20 min**. Strain, then boil down to **80 ml** (⅓ cup).
      Soften (heat, ~3 min): Stir often until the vegetables begin to brown.
        Brown (heat, ~3 min): While the chicken roasts: oil **shimmering** in a small pan, high heat. Stir often until well browned.
          - 1 Tbsp | Neutral oil
          - 1 | Chicken backbone | kept from Flatten
        Chop: Peel onion and carrot. Roughly chop all three.
          - 1 | Onion
          - 1 | Carrot
          - 1 rib | Celery
      - 1 | Bay leaf
      - 240 ml = 1 cup | Dry vermouth or sherry
      - 240 ml = 1 cup | Water
    - 1 tsp | Soy sauce
    - 45 g = 3 Tbsp | Unsalted butter
    - ¼ | Lemon | for 2 tsp juice
    - to taste | Salt & pepper
